2. Findings explaining the missing Explore screen
E-01 — Search component is missing mandatory props

ExploreScreen.tsx renders ExploreHeader without passing searchQuery, setSearchQuery, navigation/search handlers and other required callbacks.

In ExploreHeader.tsx, focusing the search field enables a branch that evaluates searchQuery.trim(). Because the supplied value is undefined, that interaction can throw a JavaScript exception and activate the ErrorBoundary.

Evidence: ExploreScreen.tsx lines 183–194; ExploreHeader.tsx lines 6–19 and 94–105



E-02 — Place validation modal has incompatible props

ExploreScreenModals passes validatingVenue, setValidatingVenue and fireHaptic to ProximityValidator.

The actual validator requires canValidateVenue, validationStatus, setValidationStatus, onClose and additional state. Those requirements are not satisfied.

Its render calls canValidateVenue(validatingVenue). Opening this modal through the affected path can throw immediately.

Evidence: ExploreScreenModals.tsx lines 76–85; ProximityValidator.tsx lines 11–48



E-03 — The heatmap receives the wrong prop contract

ExploreScreen supplies coords to VenueHeatmap, but the wrapper expects userCoords, as well as other required props.

The map component includes null-safe fallbacks, so this mismatch is not by itself proof of the screenshot crash. It does establish that map position, refresh and selection wiring are incomplete.

Evidence: ExploreScreen.tsx lines 206–214; VenueHeatmap.tsx lines 5–42



E-04 — The proximity banner is disconnected

ExploreScreen supplies venues, coords, scannedVenues and proximityDismissed, while ExploreProximityBanner expects a computed closestVenue and isDismissed.

With no closestVenue, its guard returns null. The approved Waze-style proximity banner can therefore disappear rather than show the relevant Place.

Evidence: ExploreScreen.tsx lines 169–181; ExploreProximityBanner.tsx lines 6–30



Crash conclusion: E-01 and E-02 provide concrete, source-proven exception paths. But I cannot identify which one produced your exact screenshot without the browser's exception/component stack. I will not label either as the confirmed incident root cause.
