A particularly important source-truth problem
In useExploreRadar.ts, lines 236–266, when Overpass returns no usable results, the application creates fictional venue names such as Artisanal Burger Loft or Sonic Wave Underground, assigning random coordinates.

That conflicts directly with GEO-004 and Master Plan S07, which require truthful error, cached, empty or partial-result states.

Similarly, CreateTrailModal.tsx calls trailsDomain.createTrail() and subsequently calls onSubmitTrail(), which is connected to useVibeTrails.createTrail(). Both paths can write the Trail record through their respective implementations. This violates the required single canonical writer and needs test-first reconciliation.
